Reading: closure ~1 in all terciles -> the bin-level calibration is not S/N dependent, and lower amplitudes in the high-S/N tercile reflect the galaxies themselves (compare logM_med). Closure > 1 in the low-S/N tercile -> the noise correction is incomplete there. A value of 0.000 in Part 2 means that the median of the tercile lies at or below the noise floor of that tercile (amplitude not measurable at that S/N), not that the amplitude is zero.

